---
// Prospective students and postdocs, and how to get in touch. Wording approved by Matthew on
// 2026-10-18 (drafted from his notes: motivated undergraduates welcome; graduate students through
// the SAO Predoctoral Program; not hiring postdocs directly, but CfA prize fellows can work with
// anyone at the CfA). The CfA programme pages and the fellowship-independence wording were checked
// on 2026-10-18. Linked from About, People and Open problems, not from the navigation.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHero from '../components/SectionHero.astro';
import cv from '../data/cv.json';

const root = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const cfa = 'https://www.cfa.harvard.edu/opportunities';
const fellow = `${cfa}/fellowships-visiting-scientist-positions`;
const prog = `${cfa}/graduate-undergraduate-programs`;
const ext = { target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer' };
---
<BaseLayout title="Working with me" description="Research opportunities for undergraduates, graduate students and postdocs with Matthew Payne at the Minor Planet Center and the Center for Astrophysics.">
  <SectionHero eyebrow="PEOPLE · OPPORTUNITIES" title="Working with me" lead="The Minor Planet Center is part of the Smithsonian Astrophysical Observatory, at the Center for Astrophysics | Harvard & Smithsonian. Students and early-career researchers can join research there in several ways." />
  <section class="site-content rf-prose">
    <div class="content-width rf-prose-inner">
      <h2>What I can offer</h2>
      <p><b>Undergraduates.</b> I’m happy to work with motivated undergraduates on research projects. These usually sit where orbital dynamics meets real survey data: finding and linking moving objects, the dynamics of distant and resonant Solar System bodies, and planetary-defence tools. Students work in Python with real data and the Minor Planet Center’s tools, and I aim for projects that can lead to a publishable result. The CfA’s <a href={`${prog}/reu-summer-intern-program`} {...ext}>Astronomy Summer Intern Program (REU)</a> is a good way in. For recent graduates who want a year of research before applying to graduate school, there is the CfA’s post-baccalaureate programme, <a href={`${prog}/spark`} {...ext}>SPARK</a>.</p>
      <p><b>Graduate students.</b> Motivated PhD students at other universities can do all or part of their thesis research with me at the CfA through the <a href={`${prog}/predoctoral-program`} {...ext}>SAO Predoctoral Program</a>. You stay enrolled at your home university, with your home advisor, and typically spend about a year here. If that interests you, please get in touch well before the programme’s deadlines, so that we can plan a project together.</p>
      <p><b>Postdocs.</b> I’m not directly hiring postdocs at present. However, the CfA has several prize fellowships, including the <a href={`${fellow}/cfa-fellowship`} {...ext}>CfA Fellowship</a>, the <a href={`${fellow}/clay-fellowship`} {...ext}>Clay Fellowship</a> and the <a href={`${fellow}/itc-fellowship`} {...ext}>ITC Fellowship</a>. Fellows are free to pursue their own research and to work with anyone at the CfA, including me. The full list is on the CfA’s <a href={fellow} {...ext}>fellowships page</a>. I’m glad to talk to prospective applicants about possible projects.</p>
      <p>Whatever your stage, the <a href={`${root}ideas/`}>Open problems</a> page lists questions I’d be glad to work on, and you’re welcome to bring your own idea. The <a href={`${root}people/`}>People</a> page lists the students and postdocs I’ve worked with.</p>

      <h2>Reference letters</h2>
      <p>I’m happy to write letters for people I’ve worked with directly, on a research project or in a course. Please ask at least four weeks before the first deadline, and send everything in one email:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the positions or programmes, with deadlines and how letters are submitted;</li>
        <li>your CV;</li>
        <li>a draft of your research statement or application essay;</li>
        <li>a few lines reminding me what you worked on with me, and anything you’d like me to emphasise.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A short reminder a week before a deadline is welcome. If I don’t know your work well enough to write a strong letter, I’ll say so, so that you can ask someone who can.</p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>Email is best: <span class="wwm-email">{cv.email}</span>. If you’re interested in working with me, please say briefly:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>who you are and where you are in your career;</li>
        <li>which programme or fellowship you’re considering;</li>
        <li>which of my projects, papers or open problems interests you (or your own idea).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I receive a lot of email, so please don’t worry if a reply takes a week or two; a polite follow-up is fine. Questions about MPC data, submitting observations or particular objects should go to the <a href="https://minorplanetcenter.net/mpcops/contact/" {...ext}>MPC Helpdesk</a>, where the right person will see them.</p>

      <p class="wwm-more">All the CfA’s programmes, with current deadlines, are on its <a href={cfa} {...ext}>Academics &amp; Opportunities</a> page.</p>
      <p class="back-row"><a href={root}>← Return to homepage</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wwm-email { user-select: all; }
  .wwm-more { margin-top: 36px; font-size: 14px !important; }
</style>
